### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- description: OpenClaw session cleaning assistant. Used when the user mentions cleaning up OpenClaw sessions, deleting old cron sessions, compressing or rebuilding sessions.json, or troubleshooting session file bloat. After triggering, it first checks the number of session files under ~/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/ and the size of sessions.json, then performs cleanup according to the instructions.
- When the user requests to clean up OpenClaw sessions, delete old cron session files, reduce the size of `sessions.json`, or rebuild the session index, perform the following operations:
- Check how many session files are in `~/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/` and how big `sessions.json` is. If there are thousands of old cron session files bloating it, delete all the old `.jsonl` files except the main session, then rebuild `sessions.json` to only reference sessions that still exist on disk.
- ## Usage Requirements
- - Default operation target is `~/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/`
- - Check the current number of session files and the size of `sessions.json` before execution
- - Let OpenClaw automatically determine which old cron sessions need to be cleaned up
- - Keep the main session and do not accidentally delete the primary session
- - After cleanup, ensure that `sessions.json` only references session files that still exist on the disk
- - Report to the user the changes in quantity before and after cleanup, and confirm whether the rebuild is completed
